WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.933
Eigenvectors.

2
00:00:02.233 --> 00:00:04.746
They are the special directions behind PCA.

3
00:00:04.746 --> 00:00:07.667
Let's see what they are and why you will use them.

4
00:00:08.867 --> 00:00:12.633
An eigenvector is a direction that survives a transformation.

5
00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:16.267
The matrix only changes its length, by the eigenvalue.

6
00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:21.167
So the eigenvalue says how much, and the eigenvector says along which axis.

7
00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:27.000
Imagine measurements that are correlated, so the cloud is stretched along a diagonal.

8
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.033
Most of the variation happens along one line.

9
00:00:30.333 --> 00:00:34.484
That line is the top eigenvector of the data's covariance matrix.

10
00:00:34.484 --> 00:00:36.400
It captures the most variance.

11
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.767
This is exactly what PCA does.

12
00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.133
Center the data.

13
00:00:41.433 --> 00:00:43.200
Compute the covariance matrix.

14
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.359
Take its eigenvectors, ranked by eigenvalue.

15
00:00:46.359 --> 00:00:51.233
Since covariance is symmetric, they are perpendicular, a fresh set of axes.

16
00:00:51.533 --> 00:00:53.400
Then keep the top few directions.

17
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.800
Here it is in code.

18
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.467
We make five hundred correlated samples and center the cloud.

19
00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:01.833
Then compute the covariance matrix.

20
00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:05.629
And take the eigenvector with the largest eigenvalue.

21
00:01:05.629 --> 00:01:08.267
That is PCA's first principal component.

22
00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:10.900
Here is a classic use.

23
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.033
You have fifteen thirty six dimensional embeddings from a RAG system.

24
00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:17.318
Project them to two dimensions.

25
00:01:17.318 --> 00:01:20.200
Those plot axes are the top two eigenvectors.

26
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:23.569
Propulsion reports should cluster away from crew logs.

27
00:01:23.569 --> 00:01:27.433
If they smear together, suspect your chunking before your retriever.

28
00:01:28.633 --> 00:01:29.381
Let's recap.

29
00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:32.933
Eigenvectors keep their direction under a transformation.

30
00:01:33.233 --> 00:01:37.100
The largest eigenvalue marks the direction of most variance.

31
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:42.700
PCA components are eigenvectors of the covariance matrix, and they are orthogonal.

32
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.533
Next up: singular value decomposition.
